Colour themes
=============

The built-in terminal themes reproduce the colour palettes of these projects, each under the MIT licence:
Catppuccin (catppuccin.com), Tokyo Night (github.com/enkia/tokyo-night-vscode-theme), Gruvbox
(github.com/morhetz/gruvbox), Solarized (ethanschoonover.com/solarized), Rosé Pine (rosepinetheme.com),
Dracula (draculatheme.com) and Nord (nordtheme.com). Each theme's credit is also shown in Settings.


Data and code taken from Visual Studio Code's ecosystem
=======================================================

Whiskr reads VS Code's formats natively (colour themes, TextMate grammars, language configurations, file
icon themes); it runs no extension code and downloads nothing. What it bundles is listed below with its
source, the commit it was taken at, its licence and its size. Every licence is permissive (MIT, BSD-2-Clause,
BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0, or the TextMate bundles' "permission to copy, use, modify, sell and distribute");
their full texts are at the end of this file and beside the data in each `ThirdParty/` folder, with a
manifest.json naming every file's source.

Code translated from other projects (behaviour ported to Swift, attributed in a comment in each file):

- vscode-textmate v9.3.2, https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-textmate @
